stand-debian-gpt-lvm-xfs-uefi — the REAL donor inventory captured by tools/reloca-test.sh
(phase capture) from the debian-gpt-lvm-xfs-uefi fixture VM booted into the Live under
OVMF: Debian 12 (bookworm, kernel 6.1), gpt, one 10 GiB virtio disk (vda): vda1 ESP vfat
"EFI" 512 MiB (volume id C0DE-0E5F), vda2 /boot ext4 "boot" 1 GiB, vda3 PV
(fxPV00-uefi-…) -> VG vg0: LV swap 1 GiB, LV root xfs "root" (the rest, 7.5 GiB, used
~1 GB, features CRC/FTYPE/FINOBT/SPARSE_INODES/REFLINK/INOBTCNT/BIGTIME = bookworm's
mkfs.xfs defaults, NOT nrext64); fstab /dev/mapper/vg0-* for the LVs, UUID= for /boot
and /boot/efi; systemd-networkd on ens3; grub-efi with --no-nvram (EFI/debian +
EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI). Every identifier is a constant of the fixture builder, so a
rebuild gives the same inventory (used=/min= aside). Recipient: the stand's own
recipient VM, hand-written: one 20 GiB virtio disk (serial XSRECIP0), fw=uefi, one
NIC (eth0 52:54:00:cc:dd:01 in PCI slot 7), DMI serial XS-STAND-RECIP.

Exercises the planner on inventory.sh's real LVM/XFS/ESP output: the fs and swap
records of the LVs are named by lv_path (/dev/vg0/root, /dev/vg0/swap - lsblk says
/dev/mapper/vg0-root; the inventory maps them, else "LV carries no filesystem or
swap"); the vfat volid is the eight hex digits (C0DE0E5F) for mkfs.vfat -i, not
blkid's C0DE-0E5F; R2 uefi -> uefi, R4 gpt kept with the donor's label-id and
partition GUIDs (lowercase, as lsblk prints them) and the ESP's name; R5 the ESP slot
kept in place (esp method, mkfs.vfat -F32 -i C0DE0E5F -n EFI); R7 the PV slot elastic
(20478 - 512 - 1024 = 18942 MiB = 19862126592), swap LV 1 GiB, root LV -l 100%FREE =
floor((18942 - 1024 - 4) / 4) x 4 MiB = 17912 MiB = 18782093312, block + grow; /boot
block, same size, no grow; R8 no mkfs for block volumes, the guard lists the xfs
features against 6.1 -> ok; R10 /dev/mapper/vg0-* and both UUID= specs keep (no
renumbering on gpt); R11 deb/initramfs-tools/x86_64-efi, esp=/dev/vda1,
boot=/dev/vda2, os_root=/dev/vg0/root; R12 network donor=ens3/-/networkd, one pin.
The test also runs the same donor against a bios recipient on the fly (the stand's
-r bios): gpt kept, bios_grub /dev/vda128 first, pmbr_boot=1, grub_from_live=1, the
ESP kept as a slot (WARN), the PV slot one MiB smaller (PE rounding leaves the root LV
the same).

Checked by hand against donor.inv; the plan was also what the stand's phase B applied
and transferred for real (uefi -> uefi bigger and smaller, uefi -> bios bigger: B-verify
51/51, 49/49, 51/51 on 2026-09-30/10-15).
Re-capture with: bash tools/reloca-test.sh -f debian-gpt-lvm-xfs-uefi -p capture
(writes donor.inv + raw/; expected.plan is regenerated by hand:
bash -c '. lib/common.sh; . lib/plan.sh; plan_compute DONOR RECIP auto').
